MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Servo's SVG element hierarchy had no text types at all, so <text> never
received the SVGGraphicsElement interface and getBBox was not a function
on it. That is where Mermaid died: it measures every label with getBBox
on a <text>, the first call threw, and mermaid.run bailed silently
because suppressErrors hid it.

Adds SVGTextContentElement, SVGTextPositioningElement, SVGTextElement
and SVGTSpanElement, and behind them real measurement: the element's
text is shaped with the font the cascade resolved, using the same
FontContext and Font::shape_text that HTML text goes through. So
getBBox and getComputedTextLength return real numbers -- 24 for "Mg" at
16px, 109 for "Hello diagram" -- rather than zeros. Zeros were the trap
worth avoiding: a caller that believes them lays every node out on the
same point and renders a broken diagram instead of failing honestly.

The text also paints, via vello_cpu's glyph_run, which is what canvas
already uses. Measuring without painting would have been its own
half-truth: correct layout with invisible labels.

text-anchor and dominant-baseline needed stylo-0004, being gecko-gated
like pointer-events, stop-color and stop-opacity before them -- the
fourth instance of that trap. Without text-anchor a centred label draws
left-aligned, which is most of what a diagram's labels are.

Scope is a single shaped run per <text>: no textPath, no per-glyph
x/y/rotate lists, no bidi reordering, and a <tspan> contributes its text
to the enclosing run rather than positioning itself. That is wrong for a
<tspan> carrying its own x/y and right for the commoner case of styling
part of a line.

The scene keeps its pure/coupled split: text enters it behind a
PaintText trait, so scene.rs and render.rs still depend only on kurbo
and vello_cpu and the 52-test harness still runs without building Servo.

svg/ WPT: +332 subtests against the pref-off baseline, up from +287,
with three tests moving the other way. None is a defect in this work:
  - use-element-web-animations.html fails standalone with the pref OFF
    too, so it is order-dependent flakiness in the parallel run.
  - rtl-text-path.html needs textPath, which is out of scope.
  - viewBox-scaling-text-001.html is a 1px font scaled 100x with
    combining marks, judged against a 10-pixel fuzz.
The last two were passing only because neither side rendered any text;
now one side does. That is the vacuous-reftest pattern again, and it is
progress showing up as a regression. text-transform-001 and -002 were in
the same group and are genuinely fixed, by reusing layout's own
TextTransformationIterator so SVG casing matches HTML casing exactly.

Mermaid still does not render, and the reason has moved: it now dies on
getBBox on a <foreignObject>, in both htmlLabels modes. foreignObject is
the inverse hinge the plan defers, so this does not chase it.
